The copy constructor already copies both vectors member-wise, and an empty vector copy does not allocate. There is no real speedup available here, so expect timing to stay about the same.

The rewrite below is behaviorally identical. It default-constructs `stringIndexes` and copies it only when the source is non-empty. This skips the empty-vector copy-construction path, which is the common case for non-string fields.

```cpp
FieldBase::FieldBase(const FieldBase &field)
    : values(field.values), stringIndexes()
{
    if (!field.stringIndexes.empty())
        stringIndexes = field.stringIndexes;
}
```